  "content": [
    {
      "text": "tree of life, and eat, and live for ever, Gen. 3:22 (Moses 4:28). there shall no man see me, and live, Ex. 33:20. keep my statutes … which if a man do, he shall live in them, Lev. 18:5 (Rom. 10:5; Gal. 3:12). when he beheld the serpent of brass, he lived, Num. 21:9. God doth talk with man, and he liveth, Deut. 5:24. man doth not live by bread, Deut. 8:3 (Matt. 4:4; Luke 4:4). If a man die, shall he live again, Job 14:14. I know that my redeemer liveth, Job 19:25. That he should still live for ever, and not see corruption, Ps. 49:9. What man is he that liveth, and shall not see death, Ps. 89:48. I will sing unto the Lord as long as I live, Ps. 104:33. Forsake the foolish, and live, Prov. 9:6. Live joyfully with the wife whom thou lovest, Eccl. 9:9. Thy dead men shall live, Isa. 26:19. come unto me: hear, and your soul shall live, Isa. 55:3. said unto me, Son of man, can these bones live, Ezek. 37:3. we shall live in his sight, Hosea 6:2. Israel, Seek ye me, and ye shall live, Amos 5:4. Seek good, and not evil, that ye may live, Amos 5:14. the just shall live by his faith, Hab. 2:4 (Rom. 1:17; Gal. 3:11; Heb. 10:38).",
